{"paper": "SSC-GD-19-Feb-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "In a fraction, the numerator is increased by 40% and the denominator is diminished by 20%. What fraction of the original is the new fraction?", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": true}, {"text": "7.7", "added": true}, {"text": "6.3", "added": true}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "7/4"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A motor car goes to a place at a speed of 23 km/h and returns at a speed of 33 km/h. The average speed (in km/h) of the motor car in the entire journey is:", "options": [{"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "24.3", "added": true}, {"text": "29.7", "added": true}, {"text": "28", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "27 3/28"}, {"n": 3, "text": "The smallest natural number which is divisible by 48, 72, 16 and 15 is:", "options": [{"text": "751", "added": false}, {"text": "720", "added": false}, {"text": "710", "added": false}, {"text": "784", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "720"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The LCM of 21, 24, 104 and 312 is:", "options": [{"text": "2184", "added": false}, {"text": "2253", "added": false}, {"text": "2229", "added": false}, {"text": "2149", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "2184"}, {"n": 5, "text": "100 guavas were bought at ₹1210 per hundred and were sold at a profit of ₹965. Find the selling price (in ₹) per dozen of guavas.", "options": [{"text": "256", "added": false}, {"text": "266", "added": false}, {"text": "261", "added": false}, {"text": "271", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": "261"}, {"n": 6, "text": "The population of a district is 335000, out of which 214000 are males. 31% of the population is literate. If 31% males are literate, then what percentage of females are literate?", "options": [{"text": "31%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "33%", "added": false}, {"text": "28%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "31%"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The fourth proportional to 2.5, 9.6 and 75 is:", "options": [{"text": "212", "added": false}, {"text": "288", "added": false}, {"text": "198", "added": false}, {"text": "232", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "288"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The fourth proportional to 16, a and 9a is 324. What is the value of a?", "options": [{"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "24"}, {"n": 9, "text": "When difference between compound and simple interest for three years is ₹217 at 10% interest per annum, the principal is ₹______", "options": [{"text": "7420", "added": false}, {"text": "6425", "added": false}, {"text": "8200", "added": false}, {"text": "7000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "7000"}, {"n": 10, "text": "The average weight of Mohan, Mohammad and Ashish is 46 kg. If the average weight of Mohan and Mohammad be 39 kg and that of Mohammad and Ashish be 47 kg, then the weight of Mohammad (in kg) is:", "options": [{"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "34"}, {"n": 11, "text": "Veer has ₹1224 with him. He divided it amongst his sons Nitin and Pravin and asked them to invest it at 4% rate of interest compounded annually. It was seen that Nitin and Pravin got same amount after 19 and 20 years respectively. How much (in ₹) did Veer give to Pravin?", "options": [{"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "624", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}, {"text": "724", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-instalments", "key_answer": "600"}, {"n": 12, "text": "Three-eighth of a journey is covered at a speed of 60 km/hr, and the remaining distance is covered at the rate of 40 km/hr. The average speed for the whole journey (in km/hr, rounded off to the nearest integer) is:", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "46"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The curved surface area of a sphere is 9856 cm2, find its diameter in m.", "options": [{"text": "2.8", "added": false}, {"text": "0.28", "added": false}, {"text": "5.6", "added": false}, {"text": "0.56", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": "0.56"}, {"n": 14, "text": "The cost price of 12 pens is equal to the selling price of 9 pens. Find the profit percentage.", "options": [{"text": "36.3", "added": true}, {"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": true}, {"text": "29.7", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "33 1/3%"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The simple interest on a principal amount (in ₹) is ₹487 for a period of 2 years at the rate of 5% per annum. The principal amount (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "4870", "added": false}, {"text": "4877", "added": false}, {"text": "4861", "added": false}, {"text": "4873", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": "4870"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The population of a district is 335000, out of which 214000 are males. 31% of the population is literate. If 31% males are literate, then what percentage of females are literate?", "options": [{"text": "31%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "33%", "added": false}, {"text": "28%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": "31 17/25 days"}, {"n": 17, "text": "Evaluate: (-9) - (-60) ÷ (-15) + (-2) × 7", "options": [{"text": "-27", "added": false}, {"text": "-29", "added": false}, {"text": "-30", "added": false}, {"text": "-26", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "-27"}, {"n": 18, "text": "An article is marked at ₹950. If it is sold at a discount of 20%, then the selling price becomes 2.5 times of its cost price. What is the cost price?", "options": [{"text": "₹318", "added": false}, {"text": "₹304", "added": false}, {"text": "₹312", "added": false}, {"text": "₹299", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹304"}, {"n": 19, "text": "Evaluate: 16 + 9 ÷ 3 - 3 × 3", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "10"}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": "18"}]}